  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday morning through next Sunday)\nIssued at 151 PM EDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nAutumn, it would appear, is here to stay for a while. High pressure \nover the southeast is expected to spin in place through the rest of \nthe work week and into the weekend. No sign of precipitation in any \nof the models isn't expected to do us any favors when it comes to \nthe drought monitor going forwards. As the days grow shorter and the \nleaves drop, we'll need to be mindful of the combination of dry \nfuels and low relative humidity as we being our fall Fire Season.\n\nTemperatures during the daytime will climb into the low to mid 70s \nacross most of the CWA with winds out of the ENE. Gusty conditions \nare expected to return this weekend with sustained winds around 10-\n15 mph gusting up to 20 mph. Overnight lows are expected to fall \ninto the mid to low 40s for the remainder of the week, making the \nmornings feel especially crisp.",
